# An allowlist: Docker uploads the whole context before any COPY runs, so
# everything not re-included below stays on the host -- tests, docs, .git and
# a real .env included.
*

!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!README.md
!alembic.ini
!src
!src/**

# The console stage's sources. `npm ci` and `vite build` rebuild
# node_modules and dist inside the image, so neither is sent.
!web
!web/**

# Re-excluded after the allowlist, since the last matching pattern wins:
# host bytecode and web build output under the re-included trees would
# otherwise make the image depend on the builder's working tree.
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
web/node_modules
web/dist
web/dist-fixtures
web/coverage
web/test-results
web/playwright-report
web/.vite
